<h1>SQUADUP — Full Project Architecture, File Inventory & Cloud/Cortex Migration Guide</h1>
<p><strong>Target Ingestion:</strong> Claude, Codex, Cloud Backends, Cortex Event Platforms<br>
<strong>Platform:</strong> React Native / Expo SDK 57 / TypeScript / Web & Native Mobile<br>
<strong>Directory:</strong> <code>C:\Users\HP\.gemini\antigravity\scratch\kickoff-match-app\</code></p>

<div class="note">
  <strong>Summary:</strong> This document contains an exhaustive breakdown of all 70+ files in the repository, the complete screen and navigation graph, state providers, multiplayer synchronization, 1080&times;1920 (9:16) Wrapped modules, database models, and cloud migration endpoints.
</div>

<h2>1. Executive Summary & Tech Stack</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>React Native:</strong> 0.86.3 | <strong>React:</strong> 19.2.3 | <strong>Expo SDK:</strong> 57.0.20</li>
  <li><strong>Web Support:</strong> react-native-web 0.21.2</li>
  <li><strong>TypeScript:</strong> 6.0.3 (Strict mode, 0 type errors)</li>
  <li><strong>Navigation:</strong> React Navigation 7.x (Native Stack + Bottom Tabs)</li>
  <li><strong>UI & Graphics:</strong> react-native-svg, expo-linear-gradient, @expo-google-fonts/zen-dots, @expo/vector-icons</li>
  <li><strong>Local State:</strong> AsyncStorage, singleton reactive stores (TournamentStore), Context API, Web BroadcastChannel</li>
</ul>

